# Deliberately NOT `node_modules/`. A trailing slash restricts a pattern to
# DIRECTORIES, and a symlink pointing at a directory is not a directory for that
# purpose -- so the slashed form does not ignore the shared, symlinked
# node_modules that worktrees here are set up with, and `git status` in one
# reports `?? node_modules`. Leave this entry unslashed.
node_modules
dist/
/cli
/cli-dev
/cli-dev.next
/cli-dev.next.tmp
openclaw/
CLAUDE.md
AXA.local.md
*.bun-build
.bun-build-active/
.idea/
conversation-backup.jsonl
.claude/
# The config dir is deliberately NOT published. It holds AXA.md, the agent
# definitions, the skills and the shared agent-memory, and none of that goes to
# the remote. This reverses the choice made in bfa1f32 and it is not an
# oversight -- do not "fix" it by tracking the directory again.
#
# Known cost, stated so nobody has to rediscover it: an ignored AND untracked
# path is invisible to BOTH search instruments. rg and the Grep tool obey
# .gitignore, and git grep reads the index, so neither can see anything under
# .axa/. A "no matches" result from either says nothing about this directory.
# To search it, use the filesystem directly (find / ls -R / Read), which is
# derived from neither view. A claim about .axa/ that rests on a clean grep is
# not evidence.
.axa/
.axa-install.json
.axa-update.json
.axa-update.json.lock
